==Production==
<!-- DO NOT remove the fact that this film and the Deadpool film series began as a part of 20th Century Fox's X-Men film series. This is important for the production section so the readers notice the shift between universes -->
As a part of {{WPS|20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox}}'s {{WPS|X-Men (film series)|''X-Men'' film series}}, the ''Deadpool'' film series began with the release of ''{{WPS|Deadpool (film)|Deadpool}}'' on February 12, 2016. A sequel, ''{{WPS|Deadpool 2}}'', was released on May 18, 2018.

On December 14, 2017, {{WPS|The Walt Disney Company}} announced {{WPS|Acquisition of 21st Century Fox by Disney|plans to acquire}} {{WPS|21st Century Fox}}. The acquisition would provide Disney with the opportunity to reunite the [[X-Men]], [[Fantastic Four]], and [[Deadpool]] with the Marvel family under one roof.<ref>[https://www.thewaltdisneycompany.com/walt-disney-company-acquire-twenty-first-century-fox-inc-spinoff-certain-businesses-52-4-billion-stock-2/ The Walt Disney Company To Acquire Twenty-First Century Fox, Inc., After Spinoff Of Certain Businesses, For $52.4 Billion In Stock]</ref> That same day, [[Bob Iger]] revealed that Deadpool would be a part of the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] after the acquisition was complete<ref>[https://deadline.com/2017/12/disney-fox-deal-bob-iger-digital-future-hulu-and-2b-cost-savings-1202226884/ Disney-Fox Deal: Bob Iger Discusses Digital Future, James Murdoch, Hulu and $2B Cost Savings]</ref> and that future Deadpool films could be rated R.<ref>[https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/deadpool-will-stay-r-rated-fox-disney-merger-1067651/ ‘Deadpool’ Can Stay R-Rated at Disney, Says Bob Iger]</ref>

On March 20, 2019, The Walt Disney Company’s acquisition of 21st Century Fox became effective.<ref>[https://www.thewaltdisneycompany.com/disneys-acquisition-of-21st-century-fox-will-bring-an-unprecedented-collection-of-content-and-talent-to-consumers-around-the-world/ Disney’s Acquisition of 21st Century Fox Will Bring an Unprecedented Collection of Content and Talent to Consumers Around the World]</ref> As a result, all ''X-Men'' related films that were in development, including Fox's version of ''Deadpool 3'', were put "on hold"<ref>[https://collider.com/fox-marvel-movies-status-update-lauren-shuler-donner/ Lauren Shuler Donner Confirms Fox Marvel Movies on Hold; Wants ‘X-Men’ Franchise to “Evolve”]</ref> and eventually cancelled.<ref>[https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/new-avengers-endgame-scene-shows-captain-marvel-joining-team-1199385/ New ‘Avengers: Endgame’ Footage Hits CinemaCon]</ref>

On October 14, 2019, in an interview with ''Den of Geek'', [[Paul Wernick]] said that he and [[Rhett Reese]] were waiting for approval from [[Marvel Studios]] to begin production on the film. They also said that the film would now be able to play in the Marvel Cinematic Universe sandbox.<ref>[https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/deadpool-3-update-waiting-marvel-studios-green-light Deadpool 3 Waiting on Marvel Studios Green Light]</ref>

On December 27, 2019, [[Ryan Reynolds (actor)|Ryan Reynolds]] revealed that a third ''Deadpool'' film was in development at Marvel Studios.<ref>[https://variety.com/2019/film/news/deadpool-3-confimed-ryan-reynolds-1203452448/ Ryan Reynolds Says ‘Deadpool 3’ Is in the Works at Marvel]</ref>

On November 20, 2020, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Wendy Molyneux]] and [[Lizzie Molyneux-Logelin]] had been tapped to pen the film's script and that the film was expected to be rated R.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2020/11/deadpool-3-marvel-ryan-reynolds-the-molyneux-sequel-1234617182/ Marvel Studios And Ryan Reynolds Tap The Molyneux Sisters To Pen The Sequel]</ref>

On January 11, 2021, [[Kevin Feige]] confirmed that the film would be a part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe and that it would be rated R.<ref>[https://collider.com/deadpool-3-mcu-confirmed-r-rating-filming-details-kevin-feige-interview/ Kevin Feige Confirms ‘Deadpool 3’ Is an MCU Movie; Teases R-Rating and When It’s Filming]</ref>

On March 11, 2022, ''The Hollywood Reporter'' reported that [[Shawn Levy]] would be directing the film and that Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick were now writing the film's script.<ref>[https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/deadpool-3-ryan-reynolds-shawn-levy-marvel-1235109465/ 'Deadpool 3': Shawn Levy to Direct Ryan Reynolds in Marvel Movie (Exclusive)]</ref> The following week, in an interview with ''Forbes'', Ryan Reynolds revealed that his production company {{WPS|Maximum Effort}}, would be a part of the film's producing team.<ref>[https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffconway/2022/03/15/ryan-reynolds-on-how-mntn-and-maximum-effort-are-changing-the-advertising-world-as-we-know-it/?sh=11da72444ae3 Ryan Reynolds On How MNTN And Maximum Effort Are Changing The Advertising World As We Know It]</ref>

On September 27, 2022, Ryan Reynolds announced that [[Hugh Jackman]] would be reprising his role as [[Wolverine|James Howlett/Logan/Wolverine]] from 20th Century Fox's ''X-Men'' film series in the film. It was also announced that the film would be released on September 6, 2024.<ref>[https://twitter.com/VancityReynolds/status/1574865217141481477 Ryan Reynolds on Twitter - September 27, 2022]</ref> The following month, it was announced that the film had been pushed back from its initial release date to November 8, 2024.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/marvel-studios-update-theatrical-release-schedule Marvel Studios Updates Theatrical Release Schedule]</ref>

On February 14, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Emma Corrin]] had joined the cast of the film and that they would portray the film's antagonist.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/02/deadpool-3-emma-corrin-lands-lead-role-in-marvel-studios-sequel-1235258306/ ‘Deadpool 3’: Emma Corrin Lands Lead Role In Marvel Studios Sequel]</ref>

On March 28, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Matthew Macfadyen]] had joined the cast of the film in an undisclosed role.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/03/successions-matthew-macfadyen-marvels-deadpool-3-1235310482/ ‘Succession’s Matthew Macfadyen Joins Marvel’s ‘Deadpool 3’]</ref> The next day, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Karan Soni]] and [[Leslie Uggams]] would be reprising their roles as [[Dopinder]] and [[Blind Al|Althea/Blind Al]], respectively, from the previous ''Deadpool'' films in the film.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/03/karan-soni-leslie-uggams-deadpool-1235312293/ Karan Soni And Leslie Uggams Returning For Next ‘Deadpool’ Installment]</ref>

On April 12, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Morena Baccarin]] and [[Stefan Kapičić]] would be reprising their roles as [[Vanessa Carlysle]] and [[Colossus|Piotr Rasputin/Colossus]], respectively, from the previous ''Deadpool'' films in the film.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/04/morena-baccarin-stefan-kapicic-deadpool-3-retun-vanessa-colossus-1235322308/ Morena Baccarin And Stefan Kapicic To Return For ‘Deadpool 3’ As Vanessa And Colossus]</ref>

On May 1, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Rob Delaney]] would be reprising his role as [[Peter Wisdom]] from ''Deadpool 2'' in the film.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/05/deadpool-3-rob-delaney-to-return-as-x-force-member-peter-1235351790/ ‘Deadpool 3’: Rob Delaney To Return As Human X-Force Member Peter]</ref>

On May 15, 2023, it was reported that the working title of the film was ''"Tidal Wave"''.<ref>[https://www.thecosmiccircus.com/first-report-deadpool-3-working-title-hints-at-films-story/ First Report: ‘Deadpool 3’ Working Title Hints at Film’s Story]</ref>

On May 18, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that [[Brianna Hildebrand]] would be reprising her role as [[Negasonic Teenage Warhead|Eloise Phimister/Negasonic Teenage Warhead]] from the previous ''Deadpool'' films in the film and that [[Shioli Kutsuna]] would be reprising her role as [[Yukio]] from ''Deadpool 2'' in the film.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/05/deadpool-3-brianna-hildebrand-shioli-kutsuna-back-for-marvel-threequel-1235370709/ ‘Deadpool 3’: Brianna Hildebrand & Shioli Kutsuna Set To Return For Marvel Threequel]</ref>

On May 22, 2023, it was reported that the film had begun production in {{WPS|London}}.<ref>[https://movieweb.com/deadpool-3-filming-start/ Deadpool 3 Officially Starts Filming]</ref><ref>[https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/marvel-delays-thunderbolts-filming-amid-writers-strike-1235501482/ Marvel Delays ‘Thunderbolts’ Filming Amid Writers Strike]</ref>

On June 13, 2023, it was announced that the film had been pushed up from its November 8, 2024 release date to May 3, 2024.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/marvel-studios-announces-updates-to-theatrical-release-schedule Marvel Studios Announces Updates to Theatrical Release Schedule]</ref>

On July 7, 2023, ''The Hollywood Reporter'' reported that [[Jennifer Garner]] would be reprising her role as Elektra from the 20th Century Fox films ''{{WPS|Daredevil (film)|Daredevil}}'' and ''{{WPS|Elektra (2005 film)|Elektra}}'' in the film.<ref>[https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/deadpool-3-jennifer-garner-returning-as-elektra-1235530539/ Jennifer Garner Returning as Elektra for ‘Deadpool 3’ (Exclusive)]</ref>

On July 10, 2023, Shawn Levy revealed that [[Rob Simonsen]] would be composing the score for the film.<ref>[https://twitter.com/ShawnLevyDirect/status/1678448905753698304 Shawn Levy on Twitter - July 10, 2023]</ref>

On July 14, 2023, ''Variety'' reported that the production of the film had been shut down due to the {{WPS|2023 SAG-AFTRA strike}} and that the film would resume production after the strike was resolved.<ref>[https://variety.com/2023/film/news/deadpool-3-stops-filming-actors-strike-1235668880/ ‘Deadpool 3’ Stops Production Due to SAG-AFTRA Strike]</ref>

On October 19, 2023, ''Deadline'' reported that the film would not be released on May 3, 2024.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2023/10/deadpool-3-release-date-change-actors-strike-1235577067/ ‘Deadpool 3’: Merc With A Mouth Moving Off May Release Date As Actors Strike Shakes Up 2024 Theatrical Schedule – The Dish]</ref>

On November 9, 2023, ''Variety'' reported that the film would resume production before November 23.<ref>[https://variety.com/2023/film/news/deadpool-3-restart-filming-actors-strike-1235786121/ ‘Deadpool 3’ to Restart Filming Before Thanksgiving Following End of SAG-AFTRA Strike]</ref> That same day, it was announced that the film had been pushed back from its May 3, 2024 release date to July 26, 2024.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/marvel-studios-theatrical-release-schedule-2024-2025 Marvel Studios Updates Theatrical Release Schedule]</ref> Furthermore, Ryan Reynolds revealed that [[Dogpool]] would appear in the film<ref>[https://www.instagram.com/p/CzbF4OkujPV/ Ryan Reynolds on Instagram - November 9, 2023]</ref> and that she would be portrayed by [[Peggy]].<ref>[https://www.hulldailymail.co.uk/whats-on/film/britains-ugliest-dog-peggy-star-8899397 Britain's 'ugliest dog' Peggy to star with Ryan Reynolds in Deadpool 3 movie]</ref>

On January 24, 2024, Ryan Reynolds announced that the film had wrapped production<ref>[https://twitter.com/VancityReynolds/status/1750192380563583406 Ryan Reynolds on Twitter - January 24, 2024]</ref> and Shawn Levy revealed that the post-production of the film would begin the next day.<ref>[https://twitter.com/ShawnLevyDirect/status/1750201416465969257 Shawn Levy on Twitter - January 24, 2024]</ref>

On February 11, 2024, it was revealed that the film had been retitled from ''Deadpool 3'' to ''Deadpool & Wolverine''.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/deadpool-and-wolverine-teaser First 'Deadpool & Wolverine' Teaser Debuts During The Big Game]</ref> That same day, it was revealed that [[Aaron Stanford]] would be reprising his role as [[Pyro|John Allerdyce/Pyro]] from the 20th Century Fox films ''{{WPS|X2 (film)|X2}}'' and ''{{WPS|X-Men: The Last Stand}}'' in the film.<ref>[https://deadline.com/2024/02/deadpool-and-wolverine-trailer-aaron-stanford-pyro-1235823561/ ‘Deadpool & Wolverine’ Trailer Reveals Return Of Aaron Stanford As Pyro]</ref>

